# Exemplar briefs are YOUR real documents - approved papers that went to a real
# executive. This repo is public, so nothing here is committed: every file is
# ignored except the README that documents what belongs in the folder.
#
# That is also what makes the folder itself committable. Git stores no empty
# directories, so this folder survives in the repo because of its README, and
# the skill installs with somewhere to put your exemplars already in place.
#
# Drop your files in here, then copy the whole skill folder to your endpoint:
#     Copy-Item -Recurse -Force .\skills\brief-writer "$env:USERPROFILE\.claude\skills"
#
# To commit one deliberately (a genuinely generic, de-identified example):
#     git add -f skills/brief-writer/exemplars/"Decision Brief - Example.md"

*
!*/
!README.md
!.gitignore
